 'baked', 'What is baked into the boot disk', {n: ['baked'], e: ['disk_baked'], fr: []}, ['baked'],\n      ['Baked-in files include the base <code>cloud-config.yaml<\/code>, <code>configure.sh<\/code>, <code>utils.sh<\/code> and <code>jupyter_notebook_config.py<\/code>. Their modification dates are the image build date. Files such as <code>mount-disk.sh<\/code> carry the boot date instead, because cloud-init writes them at boot from the baked cloud-config.', 'Also on the disk from the start: Docker, containerd, runc, nerdctl, crictl, <code>gcfsd<\/code>, and the Docker images tagged <code>:local<\/code>.'], 'b4', 'ls -la workbench/', {fl: ['disk_baked']}),\n    ST('b5', 'baked', 'The agent images are baked in too, retagged :local', {n: ['reg1', 'reg2', 'reg3', 'dstore'], e: ['r1_d', 'r2_d', 'r3_d', 'baked_dstore'], fr: []}, ['dstore', 'reg1', 'reg2', 'reg3'],\n      ['The agent, <code>gcloud<\/code>, proxy and executor images, any optional extras, the GPU installer and the metadata helper all sit in the Docker image store, retagged <code>vertex/*:local<\/code>.', 'They are <b>not pulled at boot<\/b>: the first units that need them run them immediately, before any pull happens. Their registry tags match the host image version.'], 'b5', 'docker images', {note: '<span class=\"tag inf\">inferred<\/span>\"Baked\" is concluded from the <code>:local<\/code> tags and from units running them before any pull, not from the build log.', fl: ['r1_d', 'r2_d', 'r3_d']}),\n    ST('b6', 'at boot', 'One image is pulled at boot: the Jupyter container', {n: ['reg4', 'cstore'], e: ['r4_c'], fr: []}, ['reg4', 'cstore'],\n      ['The Jupyter image you chose (<code>YOUR_IMAGE:latest<\/code>) is the only one fetched at boot: <code>crictl pull<\/code> through the gcfs snapshotter into the containerd <code>k8s.io<\/code> store. This is typically <b>the slowest step<\/b>, often minutes for a large image.', 'Because the tag is <code>:latest<\/code>, the docs say the instance pulls a newer image on every restart, so the Jupyter image can move without a new VM image.', 'The pull uses a token from the VM service account. Public images need no role; a private repository needs Artifact Registry Reader.'], 'b6', 'pull-custom-container-payload', {fl: ['r4_c']}),\n    ST('b7', 'summary', 'Baked versus written versus pulled', {n: [], e: [], fr: []}, ['baked', 'dstore', 'cstore'],\n      ['<b>Baked:<\/b> OS, runtimes, scripts, the agent images. <b>Written at boot:<\/b> systemd units and helper scripts, from the baked cloud-config. <b>Pulled at boot:<\/b> the Jupyter image only.', 'Versions move in lockstep for the baked parts (one build tag) and float for the pulled one (<code>:latest<\/code>).'], 'b7', 'summary'),\n  ],\n};\n\n/* ================= scene 4: metadata ================= */\nconst SC_META = {\n  id: 'meta', tab: '4 \u00b7 Metadata', intro: 'values pumped in',\n  nodes: [\n    N('g1', 20, 30, 360, 64, 'meta', 'Identity', ['notebooks-api \u00b7 notebooks-api-version=v2 \u00b7 version', 'resource-url \u00b7 instance-region']),\n    N('g2', 20, 102, 360, 64, 'meta', 'Container', ['custom-container-payload \u00b7 custom-container-image', 'cos-update-strategy']),\n    N('g3', 20, 174, 360, 78, 'meta', 'Proxy / ingress', ['proxy-backend-id \u00b7 proxy-url \u00b7 proxy-mode', 'proxy-registration-url \u00b7 new-proxy-agent-enabled', 'service-account-mode']),\n    N('g4', 20, 260, 360, 64, 'meta', 'Lifecycle', ['idle-timeout-seconds', 'shutdown-script']),\n    N('g5', 20, 332, 360, 64, 'meta', 'Access + logging', ['enable-oslogin \u00b7 enable-guest-attributes', 'google-logging-enabled \u00b7 serial-port-logging-enable']),\n    N('g6', 20, 404, 360, 64, 'meta', 'Feature flags', ['enable-jupyterlab4 \u00b7 enable-antigravity', 'disable-swap-binaries']),\n    N('g7', 20, 476, 360, 52, 'meta', 'Reporting', ['report-event-url']),\n    N('g8', 20, 536, 360, 64, 'meta', 'user-data', ['#include file:///mnt/stateful_partition/', 'workbench/cloud-config.yaml']),\n    N(