ed on the VM resource in Compute Engine.', 'Google writes most of them; you can add more. Code on the VM reads them from a local metadata server. Nothing else reaches the VM\\'s configuration.'], 'd0', 'the idea'),\n    ST('d1', 'where it lives', 'The metadata server serves them to the VM', {n: ['server'], e: [], fr: []}, ['server'],\n      ['The VM reaches the values at <code>http://metadata.google.internal<\/code> (<code>169.254.169.254<\/code>), a link-local address. A request needs the header <code>Metadata-Flavor: Google<\/code>.', 'The values are set by the Notebooks service agent when the instance is inserted and by later <code>setMetadata<\/code> calls, plus anything you supply yourself.'], 'd1', 'curl the server'),\n    ST('d2', 'the keys', 'About two dozen keys, in eight groups', {n: ['g1', 'g2', 'g3', 'g4', 'g5', 'g6', 'g7', 'g8'], e: ['g1_s', 'g2_s', 'g3_s', 'g4_s', 'g5_s', 'g6_s', 'g7_s', 'g8_s'], fr: []}, ['g1', 'g2', 'g3', 'g4', 'g5', 'g6', 'g7', 'g8'],\n      ['Identity and product, the container image, proxy and ingress, lifecycle, access and logging, feature flags, reporting, and a single <code>user-data<\/code> key that points at a cloud-config file.', 'Only the keys you pass on your own command (for example <code>idle-timeout-seconds<\/code>) are yours. The rest are Google\\'s, and the exact set changes between image versions.'], 'd2', 'the keys', {fl: ['g1_s', 'g2_s', 'g3_s', 'g4_s', 'g5_s', 'g6_s', 'g7_s', 'g8_s']}),\n    ST('d3', 'early boot', 'user-data goes to cloud-init', {n: ['c1'], e: ['s_c1'], fr: []}, ['c1', 'g8'],\n      ['<code>user-data<\/code> is <code>#include file:///mnt/stateful_partition/workbench/cloud-config.yaml<\/code>. cloud-init reads the baked file, creates the users, and <b>writes about 20 systemd units<\/b> plus helper scripts.', 'Its last instruction runs <code>startup.sh<\/code>.'], 'd3', 'cloud-init', {fl: ['s_c1']}),\n    ST('d4', 'boot \u00b7 configure', 'workbench-configure reads the attributes', {n: ['c2'], e: ['s_c2'], fr: []}, ['c2'],\n      ['A Docker container (<code>service_generator_agent<\/code>) reads the instance attributes and writes <b><code>/tmp/ENV_INFO<\/code><\/b>, a flat <code>KEY=VALUE<\/code> file.', 'Names and values line up: <code>custom-container-payload<\/code> becomes <code>WORKBENCH_CUSTOM_CONTAINER_PAYLOAD<\/code>, <code>instance-region<\/code> becomes <code>INSTANCE_REGION<\/code>, <code>proxy-backend-id<\/code> becomes <code>BACKEND_ID<\/code>.'], 'd4', '/tmp/ENV_INFO', {note: '<span class=\"tag inf\">inferred<\/span>The agent that does the mapping is a binary that is not publicly documented. The correspondence is by name and value.', fl: ['s_c2']}),\n    ST('d5', 'boot \u00b7 container', 'ENV_INFO becomes the Jupyter container\\'s flags and environment', {n: ['c3'], e: ['s_c3'], fr: []}, ['c3', 'g2'],\n      ['systemd units load the file with <code>EnvironmentFile=/tmp/ENV_INFO<\/code> and expand it: the image to pull, <code>--user $CONTAINER_USER<\/code>, the FUSE flags, <code>-e GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT<\/code> and <code>-e GOOGLE_CLOUD_REGION<\/code>.', 'These are fixed when the container starts. The container can additionally read the metadata server itself, at any time.'], 'd5', 'jupyter-payload.service', {fl: ['s_c3']}),\n    ST('d6', 'boot \u00b7 agents', 'Proxy keys reach the proxy agent', {n: ['c4', 'c9'], e: ['s_c4', 's_c9'], fr: []}, ['c4', 'c9', 'g3'],\n      ['<code>proxy-backend-id<\/code> and <code>proxy-registration-url<\/code> become <code>BACKEND_ID<\/code> and <code>PROXY_REGISTRATION_URL<\/code>, which the proxy agent uses to register its outbound tunnel.', 'Optional extras in the image may read keys such as <code>proxy-backend-id<\/code> straight from the metadata server instead (for example to build a CORS origin): these are direct readers.'], 'd6', 'proxy-agent + extras', {fl: ['s_c4', 's_c9']}),\n    ST('d7', 'running', 'Lifecycle, reporting, access and logging keys', {n: ['c5', 'c6', 'c7', 'c8'], e: ['s_c5', 's_c6', 's_c7', 's_c8'], fr: []}, ['c5', 'c6', 'c7', 'c8', 'g4', 'g5', 'g7'],\n      ['<code>idle-timeout-seconds<\/code> drives idle shutdown (documented). <code>report-event-url<\/code> is where the health agent posts its HEALTH event.', '<code>enable-oslogin<\/code> is why you log in as an OS Login user such as <code>user_example_com<\/code>. Logging and serial-console keys feed Cloud Logging and the serial port (inferred from names). A <code>shutdown-script<\/code> key may point at a path that does not exist on a COS host: check before relying on it.'], 'd7', 'who reads what', {fl: ['s_c5', 's_c6', 's_c7', 's_c8']}),\n    ST('d8', 'reverse path', 'The VM writes back through guest attributes', {n: ['ga'], e: ['ga_s'], fr: []}, ['ga'],\n      ['Guest attributes are a write channel in the other direction: the VM puts values on the metadata server and anything with the right access can read them through the Compute API.', 'Typical namespaces include <code>notebooks/<\/code>, <code>workbench-notebooks/<\/code>, <code>hostkeys/<\/code> and <code>guest-agent/<\/code>. <code>enable-guest-attributes=TRUE<\/code> is required for idle shutdown (documented).'], 'd8', 'guest attributes', {fl: ['ga_s']}),\n    ST('d9', 'your keys', 'Adding your own values', {n: [], e: [], fr: []}, ['g2', 'g4'],\n      ['<code>container-env-file<\/code> and <code>container-custom-params<\/code> add environment variables and extra <code>nerdctl run<\/code> flags. <code>post-startup-script<\/code> (+ <code>-behavior<\/code>) adds a script to run after boot. All are documented.', 'An update (<code>gcloud workbench instances update --metadata=\u2026<\/code>) becomes a Compute <code>setMetadata<\/code> call by the service agent. Container flags are fixed at start, so expect a restart to be needed. The idle timeout is documented to apply live.'], 'd9', 'updating metadata', {note: '<span class=\"tag inf\">inferred<\/span>The restart requirement for container keys is a reasoned expectation, not a tested result.'}),\n  ],\n};\n\n/* ================= scene 5: disks ================= */\nconst SC_DISKS = {\n  id: 'disks', tab: '5 \u00b7 Disks', intro: 'partitions and mounts',\n  nodes: [\n    N('pd1', 20, 60, 250, 100, 'cloud', 'Persistent disk (boot)', ['INSTANCE-boot', 'size you choose \u00b7 pd-standard \u00b7 SCSI', 'cloned from the host image']),\n    N('pd2', 20, 380, 250, 100, 'cloud', 'Persistent disk (data)', ['INSTANCE-data-workspace', 'size you choose \u00b7 pd-standard \u00b7 SCSI', 'blank at creation']),\n    N('sda1', 310, 60, 290, 64, 'disk', 'sda1 \u00b7 most of the disk', ['stateful partition (ext4, read-write)']),\n    N('sda3', 310, 138, 290, 64, 'host', 'sda3 \u00b7 ~2 GB \u2192 vroot', ['root, read-only (dm-verity)', 'boots from vmlinuz.A']),\n    N('sda8', 310, 216, 290, 52, 'vm', 'sda8 \u00b7 small', ['OEM partition']),\n    N('sdao', 310, 282, 290, 64, 'vm', 'sda2, 4\u20137, 9\u201312', ['small COS partitions', 'roles: standard COS layout']),\n    N('sdb', 310, 380, 290, 64, 'disk', 'sdb \u00b7 ext4', ['the data disk']),\n    N('m_state', 650, 60, 300, 100, 'svc', '/mnt/stateful_partition and /var', ['most of the boot disk', 'workbench scripts, cloud-config,', 'Docker + containerd data, gcfs cache']),\n    N('m_root', 650, 174, 300, 52, 'svc', '/   (read-only)', ['~2 GB \u00b7 mostly full']),\n    N('m_oem', 650, 240, 300, 52, 'svc', '/usr/share/oem', []),\n    N('m_home', 650, 380, 300, 64, 'disk', '/home/jupyter', ['ext4 \u00b7 rw \u00b7 your workspace']),\n    N('c_agents', 990, 60, 280, 100, 'agent', 'agent containers', ['/tmp (ENV_INFO, health log)', '/mnt/stateful_partition/workbench', 'docker.sock (health-agent)']),\n    N('c_fuse', 990, 178, 280, 64, 'svc', 'gcfsd FUSE mount', ['/run/gcfsd/mnt: layers on demand']),\n    N('c_pay', 990, 370, 280, 100, 'cont', 'payload-container', ['/ = overlay on sda1', '/home/jupyter = bind mount of sdb', '/dev/shm = tmpfs']),\n    N('c_open', 990, 484, 280, 60, 'agent', 'optional extras', ['/home/jupyter = bind mount']),\n    N('summary', 310, 580, 970, 120, 'ext', 'What happens to your data', ['Survives stop and start: sdb (/home/jupyter) and the stateful partition (images, scripts, gcfs cache).', 'Recreated every start: container writable layers, /tmp/ENV_INFO, units written by cloud-init.', 'Deleted with the instance: BOTH disks (autoDelete: true), including /home/jupyter.', 'While stopped: disks stay (READY) and keep billing; compute billing stops.']),\n  ],\n  frames: [{id: 'vmE', x: 290, y: 16, w: 990, h: 548, label: 'Inside the VM', lx: 306, ly: 12}],\n  labels: [],\n  edges: [\n    E('pd1_s1', [[270, 95], [310, 92]]), E('pd1_s3', [[270, 110], [310, 170]]), E('pd1_s8', [[270, 125], [310, 242]]), E('pd1_so', [[270, 140], [310, 314]]),\n    E('pd2_sdb', [[270, 430], [310, 412]]),\n    E('s1_m', [[600, 92], [650, 92]]), E('s3_m', [[600, 170], [650, 200]]), E('s8_m', [[600, 242], [650, 266]]), E('sdb_m', [[600, 412], [650, 412]]),\n    E('state_agents', [[950, 110], [990, 110]]),\n    E('home_pay', [[950, 412], [990, 412]]),\n    E('home_open', [[950, 430], [968, 430], [968, 514], [990, 514]]),\n  ],\n  steps: [\n    ST('e0', 'idea', 'Clean slate: the VM sees two block devices', {n: [], e: [], fr: ['vmE']}, [],\n      ['Inside the VM there will be two block devices: <code>sda<\/code> (the boot disk) and <code>sdb<\/code> (the data disk). This scene shows what is on each, where it is mounted, and what each container can see.'], 'e0', 'the idea'),\n    ST('e1', 'at creation', 'Two persistent disks are attached by the insert call', {n: ['pd1', 'pd2'], e: [], fr: []}, ['pd1', 'pd2'],\n      ['The boot disk is <code>pd-standard<\/code>, cloned from the host image. The data disk is <code>pd-standard<\/code> too, and blank. You choose the sizes (for example around 150 GB and 100 GB by default).', 'Both attach over SCSI, read-write, with <b><code>autoDelete: true<\/code><\/b>. Device names are <code>boot<\/code> and <code>data-workspace<\/code>.'], 'e1', 'disks describe'),\n    ST('e2', 'boot disk', 'The boot disk is a COS partition table', {n: ['sda1', 'sda3', 'sda8', 'sdao'], e: ['pd1_s1', 'pd1_s3', 'pd1_s8', 'pd1_so'], fr: []}, ['sda1', 'sda3'],\n      ['<code>sda<\/code> has the standard COS dozen partitions. The big one, <b><code>sda1<\/code><\/b>, is the stateful partition. <b><code>sda3<\/code><\/b> (about 2 GB) is the root filesystem; the kernel command line says <code>vmlinuz.A<\/code>, so it is the active root.', 'The small ones are standard COS partitions (kernels, a second root, the OEM partition, EFI). Their roles come from the COS layout.'], 'e2', 'lsblk', {note: '<span class=\"tag inf\">inferred<\/span>Partition roles other than sda1, sda3 and sda8 come from the standard COS layout.', fl: ['pd1_s1', 'pd1_s3']}),\n    ST('e3', 'root', 'The root is read-only and verified', {n: ['m_root', 'm_oem'], e: ['s3_m', 's8_m'], fr: []}, ['m_root', 'sda3'],\n      ['<code>sda3<\/code> appears as <code>vroot<\/code>, a <b>dm-verity<\/b> device mounted at <code>/<\/code> read-only, and mostly full. There is no package manager, and nothing you install on the host would persist.', '<code>/usr/share/oem<\/code> comes from <code>sda8<\/code>.'], 'e3', 'root mount', {fl: ['s3_m']}),\n    ST('e4', 'stateful partition', 'The stateful partition holds everything that changes', {n: ['m_state', 'c_agents', 'c_fuse'], e: ['s1_m', 'state_agents'], fr: []}, ['m_state', 'c_agents'],\n      ['<code>sda1<\/code> is mounted at <code>/mnt/stateful_partition<\/code> and <code>/var<\/code>, and holds most of the boot disk.', 'It holds the Workbench scripts and cloud-config, Docker and containerd data, and the gcfs layer cache. The agent containers bind-mount parts of it (<code>/mnt/stateful_partition/workbench<\/code>, <code>/tmp<\/code>).'], 'e4', 'df + findmnt', {fl: ['s1_m', 'state_agents']}),\n    ST('e5', 'data disk', 'The data disk becomes /home/jupyter', {n: ['sdb', 'm_home'], e: ['pd2_sdb', 'sdb_m'], fr: []}, ['m_home', 'sdb', 'pd2'],\n      ['<code>workbench-mount-disk<\/code> finds <code>/dev/disk/by-id/google-data-workspace<\/code> (<code>sdb<\/code>) and mounts it at <b><code>/home/jupyter<\/code><\/b> as ext4, remounts it with <code>exec<\/code>, and changes its owner to the container user (root).', 'On first boot, the pull script also copies the Jupyter image\\'s <code>/home<\/code> content onto it. The disk is blank at creation, so something must format it; that step is not visible in the scripts (inferred).'], 'e5', 'mount-disk.sh', {fl: ['pd2_sdb', 'sdb_m']}),\n    ST('e6', 'containers', 'The containers see /home/jupyter by bind mount', {n: ['c_pay', 'c_open'], e: ['home_pay', 'home_open'], fr: []}, ['c_pay', 'c_open', 'm_home'],\n      ['<code>payload-container<\/code> bind-mounts <code>/home/jupyter<\/code> (the command line may list it more than once, harmlessly). Its root is an <b>overlay on the stateful partition<\/b>, so anything written elsewhere is lost when the container is recreated.', 'Optional extras that mount the same directory write to your data disk too.'], 'e6', 'container mounts', {fl: ['home_pay', 'home_open']}),\n    ST('e7', 'persistence', 'What survives, what is recreated, what is deleted', {n: ['summary'], e: [], fr: []}, ['summary'],\n      ['<b>Survives stop and start:<\/b> <code>/home/jupyter<\/code> and the stateful partition. <b>Recreated:<\/b> container writable layers, <code>/tmp/ENV_INFO<\/code>, units written by cloud-init.', '<b>Deleted with the instance:<\/b> both disks. <b>While stopped:<\/b> disks stay and keep billing.'], 'e7', 'summary', {warn: true, note: '<span class=\"tag warn\">heads-up<\/span>Deleting the instance deletes <code>/home/jupyter<\/code>.'}),\n  ],\n};\n\n/* ================= scene 3: boot (data defined above) ================= */\nconst SC_BOOT = {id: 'boot', tab: '3 \u00b7 Boot', intro: 'startup.sh, step by step', nodes: NODES, frames: FRAMES, labels: LABELS, edges: EDGES, steps: STEPS, segs: SEGS};\n\nconst SCENES = [SC_BUILD, SC_SUPPLY, SC_BOOT, SC_META, SC_DISKS];\n\n/* ---------------- svg scaffolding ---------------- */\nconst svg = $('#stage');\nconst el = (n, a = {}, p) => { const e = document.createElementNS(NS, n); for (const k in a) e.setAttribute(k, a[k]); if (p) p.appendChild(e); return e; };\nconst defs = el('defs', {}, svg);\nconst mk = (id) => { const m = el('marker', {id, viewBox: '0 0 10 10', refX: '8', refY: '5', markerWidth: '10', markerHeight: '10', orient: 'auto-start-reverse', markerUnits: 'userSpaceOnUse'}, defs); el('path', {d: 'M0,1 L9,5 L0,9 z', class: 'arrow'}, m); };\nmk('ar');\n\nlet frameEls = {}, nodeEls = {}, edgeEls = {}, lblEls = {}, NODE_BY_ID = {};\n\nfunction drawText(g, n, lines) {\n  g.querySelectorAll('text').forEach(t => t.remove());\n  const big = n.h > 100;\n  const t = el('text', {x: n.x + 12, y: n.y + (n.h <= 36 ? 21 : 22), class: 't'}, g); t.textContent = n.t;\n  (lines || []).forEach((s, i) => { if (!s) return; const x = el('text', {x: n.x + 12, y: n.y + 40 + i * (big ? 17 : 14), class: 's'}, g); x.textContent = s; });\n}\n\nfunction buildScene(S) {\n  Array.from(svg.childNodes).forEach(c => { if (c !== defs) svg.removeChild(c); });\n  frameEls = {}; nodeEls = {}; edgeEls = {}; lblEls = {}; NODE_BY_ID = {};\n  S.frames.forEach(f => {\n    const g = el('g', {class: 'frame', id: 'f-' + f.id}, svg);\n    el('rect', {x: f.x, y: f.y, width: f.w, height: f.h}, g);\n    const t = el('text', {x: f.lx, y: f.ly + 1}, g); t.textContent = f.label;\n    frameEls[f.id] = g;\n  });\n  S.labels.forEach(l => { const g = el('g', {class: 'lbl'}, svg); const t = el('text', {x: l.x, y: l.y}, g); t.textContent = l.text; lblEls[l.id] = g; });\n  S.edges.forEach(e => {\n    const g = el('g', {class: 'edge' + (e.sample ? ' sample' : ''), id: 'e-' + e.id}, svg);\n    const d = e.pts.map((p, i) => (i ? 'L' : 'M') + p[0] + ',' + p[1]).join(' ');\n    const path = el('path', {d, class: 'line', 'marker-end': 'url(#ar)'}, g);\n    if (e.both) path.setAttribute('marker-start', 'url(#ar)');\n    if (e.lbl) { const t = el('text', {x: e.l[0], y: e.l[1]}, g); t.textContent = e.lbl; }\n    edgeEls[e.id] = g;\n  });\n  S.nodes.forEach(n => {\n    NODE_BY_ID[n.id] = n;\n    const g = el('g', {class: 'node k-' + n.k, id: 'n-' + n.id}, svg);\n    el('rect', {x: n.x, y: n.y, width: n.w, height: n.h}, g);\n    drawText(g, n, n.s);\n    nodeEls[n.id] = g;\n  });\n}\n\n/* ---------------- state ---------------- */\nlet sc = 0, cur = 0, playing = false, timer = null, timers = [], sampleOn = $('#sample').checked;\nconst S_ = () => SCENES[sc];\nconst active = () => S_().steps.filter(s => !s.sample || sampleOn);\n\nfunction revealedUpTo(list, idx) {\n  const nodes = new Set(), edges = new Set(), frames = new Set(), set = {};\n  for (let i = 0; i <= idx; i++) {\n    const s = list[i];\n    s.r.n.forEach(x => nodes.add(x)); s.r.e.forEach(x => edges.add(x)); (s.r.fr || []).forEach(x => frames.add(x));\n    if (s.set) for (const k in s.set) set[k] = s.set[k];\n  }\n  return {nodes, edges, frames, set};\n}\n\nfunction colourTerm(txt) {\n  return txt.split('\\n').map((ln, i) => {\n    const esc = ln.replace(/&/g, '&amp;').replace(/<\/g, '&lt;').replace(/>/g, '&gt;');\n    let cls = '';\n    if (/^\\s*\\$ /.test(ln)) cls = 'c'; else if (/^\\s*#/.test(ln)) cls = 'd'; else if (/(unsecured|NO PASSWORD|DENIED)/.test(ln)) cls = 'r'; else if (/(ACTIVE|Response: <Response \\[200\\]>)/.test(ln)) cls = 'g';\n    return '<span class=\"ln ' + cls + '\" style=\"animation-delay:' + Math.min(i * 45, 900) + 'ms\">' + (esc || ' ') + '<\/span>';\n  }).join('');\n}\n\nfunction render() {\n  const S = S_(), list = active();\n  if (cur >= list.length) cur = list.length - 1;\n  const s = list[cur];\n  timers.forEach(clearTimeout); timers = [];\n  const R = revealedUpTo(list, cur);\n\n  Object.entries(frameEls).forEach(([id, g]) => g.classList.toggle('on', R.frames.has(id)));\n  Object.entries(lblEls).forEach(([id, g]) => g.classList.toggle('on', R.nodes.has(id)));\n  Object.entries(nodeEls).forEach(([id, g]) => {\n    g.classList.toggle('on', R.nodes.has(id));\n    g.classList.toggle('focus', (s.f || []).indexOf(id) >= 0);\n    const n = NODE_BY_ID[id];\n    let lines = n.s;\n    if (R.set[id] !== undefined && R.set[id] !== null) lines = R.set[id];\n    drawText(g, n, lines);\n  });\n  svg.classList.toggle('hasfocus', (s.f || []).length > 0);\n  Object.entries(edgeEls).forEach(([id, g]) => { g.classList.toggle('on', R.edges.has(id)); g.classList.remove('flow'); });\n  (s.fl || []).forEach((id, i) => {\n    const g = edgeEls[id]; if (!g) return;\n    g.classList.add('on');\n    if (s.seq) timers.push(setTimeout(() => g.classList.add('flow'), 500 + i * 650)); else g.classList.add('flow');\n  });\n\n  $('#caption').innerHTML = '<div class=\"meta\"><span class=\"pill\">' + S.tab + '<\/span><span class=\"pill\">Step ' + cur + ' of ' + (list.length - 1) + '<\/span><span class=\"pill\">' + s.time + '<\/span>' + (s.sample ? '<span class=\"tag smp\">sample<\/span>' : '') + '<\/div>' +\n    '<h3>' + s.title + '<\/h3><ul>' + s.what.map(w => '<li>' + w + '<\/li>').join('') + '<\/ul>' +\n    (s.bar ? '<div class=\"bar run\"><i><\/i><\/div><div class=\"meta\">typically minutes on a real VM, shown here in a few seconds<\/div>' : '') +\n    (s.note ? '<div class=\"callout' + (s.warn ? ' warn' : (s.sample ? ' smp' : '')) + '\"><p>' + s.note + '<\/p><\/div>' : '');\n  $('#term-title').textContent = s.evt || 'evidence';\n  $('#term').innerHTML = colourTerm(ev(s.ev));\n\n  const last = sc === SCENES.length - 1, atEnd = cur === list.length - 1;\n  $('#stepno').textContent = 'Scene ' + (sc + 1) + '/' + SCENES.length + ' \u00b7 step ' + cur + '/' + (list.length - 1);\n  $('#b-back').disabled = sc === 0 && cur === 0;\n  $('#b-next').disabled = last && atEnd;\n  $('#b-next').textContent = atEnd && !last ? 'Next scene \u25b6' : 'Next \u25b6';\n  $('#b-reset').disabled = cur === 0 && !playing;\n  $('#b-play').textContent = playing ? '\u275a\u275a Pause' : (last && atEnd ? '\u21bb Replay tour' : '\u25b6 Play');\n  document.querySelectorAll('.dot').forEach((d, i) => { d.classList.toggle('cur', i === cur); d.classList.toggle('done', i < cur); });\n  document.querySelectorAll('.tab').forEach((t, i) => t.classList.toggle('cur', i === sc));\n  $('#sample-wrap').hidden = S.id !== 'boot';\n\n  const tl = $('#timeline'); tl.hidden = !S.segs;\n  if (S.segs) {\n    const seg = s.tl, maxSeg = list.slice(0, cur + 1).reduce((m, x) => Math.max(m, x.tl), -1);\n    document.querySelectorAll('.seg').forEach((d, i) => { d.classList.toggle('cur', i === seg); d.classList.toggle('done', i < maxSeg || (i <= maxSeg && i !== seg)); });\n  }\n  const tn = $('#timeline-note'); if (tn) tn.hidden = !S.segs;\n}\n\nfunction buildDots() {\n  const list = active(); const box = $('#dots'); box.innerHTML = '';\n  list.forEach((s, i) => {\n    const b = document.createElement('button'); b.className = 'dot' + (s.sample ? ' smp' : ''); b.type = 'button'; b.textContent = i; b.title = i + '. ' + s.title; b.setAttribute('aria-label', 'Step ' + i + ': ' + s.title);\n    b.addEventListener('click', () => { stop(); cur = i; render(); });\n    box.appendChild(b);\n  });\n}\nfunction buildTabs() {\n  const t = $('#tabs'); t.innerHTML = '';\n  SCENES.forEach((S, i) => {\n    const b = document.createElement('button'); b.type = 'button'; b.className = 'tab'; b.innerHTML = '<b>' + S.tab + '<\/b><span>' + S.intro + '<\/span>';\n    b.addEventListener('click', () => { stop(); setScene(i, 0); });\n    t.appendChild(b);\n  });\n}\nfunction buildTimeline(S) {\n  const t = $('#timeline'); t.innerHTML = '';\n  (S.segs || []).forEach(s => { const d = document.createElement('div'); d.className = 'seg' + (s.c ? ' ' + s.c : ''); d.innerHTML = '<b>' + s.t + '<\/b>' + s.d; t.appendChild(d); });\n}\nfunction setScene(i, step) {\n  sc = i; buildScene(S_()); buildTimeline(S_()); buildDots();\n  const n = active().length;\n  cur = step === 'last' ? n - 1 : Math.min(step, n - 1);\n  render();\n}\n\n/* ---------------- controls ---------------- */\nfunction stop() { playing = false; clearTimeout(timer); timer = null; }\nfunction advance() {          // returns false when the whole tour is finished\n  const n = active().length;\n  if (cur < n - 1) { cur++; render(); return true; }\n  if (sc < SCENES.length - 1) { setScene(sc + 1, 0); return true; }\n  return false;\n}\nfunction tick() {\n  if (!playing) return;\n  if (!advance()) { stop(); render(); return; }\n  const s = active()[cur];\n  timer = setTimeout(tick, +$('#speed').value + (s.bar ? 1500 : 0) + (cur === 0 ? 800 : 0));\n}\nfunction play() {\n  if (playing) { stop(); render(); return; }\n  const last = sc === SCENES.length - 1;\n  if (last && cur === active().length - 1) setScene(0, 0);\n  playing = true; render();\n  timer = setTimeout(tick, cur === 0 ? 1200 : +$('#speed').value);\n}\n$('#b-play').addEventListener('click', play);\n$('#b-next').addEventListener('click', () => { stop(); advance(); render(); });\n$('#b-back').addEventListener('click', () => {\n  stop();\n  if (cur > 0) { cur--; render(); }\n  else if (sc > 0) setScene(sc - 1, 'last');\n});\n$('#b-reset').addEventListener('click', () => { stop(); cur = 0; render(); });\n$('#sample').addEventListener('change', e => {\n  const keyBefore = active()[cur] && active()[cur].key;\n  sampleOn = e.target.checked; stop(); buildDots();\n  const list = active(); const i = list.findIndex(s => s.key === keyBefore); cur = i >= 0 ? i : Math.min(cur, list.length - 1); render();\n});\ndocument.addEventListener('keydown', e => {\n  if (['INPUT', 'SELECT', 'TEXTAREA'].indexOf(e.target.tagName) >= 0) return;\n  const demo = $('#demo').getBoundingClientRect();\n  if (demo.bottom < 0 || demo.top > innerHeight) return;\n  if (e.key === ' ') { e.preventDefault(); play(); }\n  else if (e.key === 'ArrowRight') { e.preventDefault(); $('#b-next').click(); }\n  else if (e.key === 'ArrowLeft') { e.preventDefault(); $('#b-back').click(); }\n  else if (e.key === 'Home') { e.preventDefault(); $('#b-reset').click(); }\n});\n\nfunction pinSide() {\n  const bar = $('#controls'), side = $('#side'); if (!bar || !side) return;\n  const top = 52 + bar.offsetHeight + 24;\n  side.style.top = top + 'px'; side.style.maxHeight = 'calc(100vh - ' + (top + 16) + 'px)';\n}\nwindow.addEventListener('resize', pinSide);\nbuildTabs(); setScene(0, 0); pinSide();\nwindow.__demo = {\n  scenes: () => SCENES.length, scene: () => sc, steps: () => active().length,\n  setScene: (i, j) => { stop(); setScene(i, j || 0); }, go: i => { stop(); cur = i; render(); },\n  state: () => ({sc, cur, playing}),\n};\n})();\n<\/script><\/body><\/html>";</script>
